  - itemName: KeyCard
    itemSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ce2098a822552e64c98fbedce8314606, type: 3}
    itemDescription: I think I've seen a digital reader somewhere near.
    itemImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ce2098a822552e64c98fbedce8314606, type: 3}
    showTooltipSprite: 0
  - itemName: Crowbar
    itemSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b8879d3b9146a7e42b6a57a62e8f9da2, type: 3}
    itemDescription: Maybe I can use this to force open something.
    itemImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b8879d3b9146a7e42b6a57a62e8f9da2, type: 3}
    showTooltipSprite: 0
  - itemName: Slide-tape
    itemSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4470bf318ca10a34a95475b15c6cdce7, type: 3}
    itemDescription: '"The story of our town", what is this about? If I could find
      a projector I would be able to watch this.'
    itemImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4470bf318ca10a34a95475b15c6cdce7, type: 3}
    showTooltipSprite: 0
  - itemName: Deer Totem
    itemSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: a4101ff1ed0a72340ac33bb95ce53397, type: 3}
    itemDescription: A deer totem carved on hickory wood. For some reason, you are
      drawn to hold it close to your chest and a sense of gentleness fills you from
      within.
    itemImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: a4101ff1ed0a72340ac33bb95ce53397, type: 3}
    showTooltipSprite: 0
  - itemName: Bear Totem
    itemSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7568c1435ece2f94d8885a2bb1a54391, type: 3}
    itemDescription: A bear totem carved on hickory wood. As you hold it firmly in
      your hand, you can feel a new-found source of courage that is born within your
      heart and flows to every inch of your soul.
    itemImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7568c1435ece2f94d8885a2bb1a54391, type: 3}
    showTooltipSprite: 0
  - itemName: Owl Totem
    itemSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 01bda8a155465dd4a905fbdfb9c8b908, type: 3}
    itemDescription: An owl totem carved on hickory wood. When you look at it, you
      are reminded of all the things you still do not know and yearn to learn about,
      but there is no feeling of impatience. You know that anything can be found
      at the right time and place when you most need it.
    itemImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 01bda8a155465dd4a905fbdfb9c8b908, type: 3}
    showTooltipSprite: 0
  - itemName: Great Feather
    itemSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 3d73ed14abfe951428fe6894ce8067f1, type: 3}
    itemDescription: A red and golden feather, larger than your own arm.
    itemImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 3d73ed14abfe951428fe6894ce8067f1, type: 3}
    showTooltipSprite: 0
  - itemName: Claw Pendant
    itemSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 86fe0009ed89bef458e05aebc9f3d692, type: 3}
    itemDescription: A simple pendant made with a leather cord from which hangs a
      wolf claw and a crow feather. It was given by your mother as a lucky charm
      that would keep you safe.
    itemImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 86fe0009ed89bef458e05aebc9f3d692, type: 3}
    showTooltipSprite: 0
  - itemName: Diary Entry 1
    itemSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4d9a8f166b8868042b3a97d688f4f734, type: 3}
    itemDescription: '10/30/xxxx - The town does not feel safe any more. There is
      something in the air. Something cold and heavy. Something unearthly. There
      are rumours of shadows moving at the corner of the eye, of voices calling you
      in the night. There is a fuss among the spirits, they are becoming more and
      more anxious. I fear some have started to prey on us. I see them too, sneaking
      between the buildings, hovering just outside my door. Have they finally grown
      impatient with us? Have we done something to disturb the balance? I do not
      know what to do, but I must protect my son. '
    itemImage: {fileID: 0}
    showTooltipSprite: 0
  - itemName: Diary Entry 2
    itemSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4d9a8f166b8868042b3a97d688f4f734, type: 3}
    itemDescription: "11/13/xxxx - More and more people speak of nightmares. I ran
      into our neighbour next-door today. She looked pale, with dark circles under
      her eyes. When I asked her, she told me she hears something whispering to her
      at night, twisting her dreams into terrors. Her hands trembled as she told
      me this. The poor woman believes she is going crazy. But she is not the only
      one. Every day, I see others with that same look in their eyes \u2013 tired,
      hollow, gone. The spirits do not simply walk among us no more; they are creeping
      into our minds. The hissing sounds, I hear them too. But, I must resist. I
      cannot let them in."
    itemImage: {fileID: 0}
    showTooltipSprite: 0
  - itemName: Diary Entry 3
    itemSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4d9a8f166b8868042b3a97d688f4f734, type: 3}
    itemDescription: 12/03/xxxx - I am afraid. My husband has started changing. He
      no longer looks at me the way he used to do. His eyes have turned darker and
      something corrupt lingers within them. He disappears at night, claiming he
      is only going to get some air. But when he returns, his clothes are damp with
      the morning dew, his breath heavy with something foul. I caught a glimpse of
      his reflection in the window last night. What I saw made my heart stop for
      a second. Horns curling from his head and scales falling from his skin. It
      must have been a hallucination. I do not want to believe it, but I cannot stop
      doubting him. Something is wrong. Something heinous is happening to him.
    itemImage: {fileID: 0}
    showTooltipSprite: 0
  - itemName: Diary Entry 4
    itemSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4d9a8f166b8868042b3a97d688f4f734, type: 3}
    itemDescription: "12/27/xxxx - I confronted him today. I begged him to tell me
      the truth, to let me help him. He only stared at me with those empty eyes and
      said, with a faltering voice: \u201CIt is too late now\u201D. He spoke of hunger,
      of the whispers growing louder, of a force greater than himself pulling him
      into a void and stripping him of his humanity. A tear slipped down his face
      as he pronounced every word. I knew then that I had lost him to the shadows.
      My love is no longer the man I once knew. His body was now controlled by something
      else. A monster. Are we going to be next? I cannot let anything happen to my
      son. He is still young, but he must understand \u2013 I must tell him everything
      soon. "
    itemImage: {fileID: 0}
    showTooltipSprite: 0
  - itemName: Diary Entry 5
    itemSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4d9a8f166b8868042b3a97d688f4f734, type: 3}
    itemDescription: '01/12/xxxx - The whispers have grown louder; I cannot silence
      them anymore. They are calling me now, and they will not stop until they have
      me. My reflection is not my own; I barely recognize it. I see flickers of green
      on my skin, and my vision is getting blurrier. I feel like I am drowning in
      the darkness, little by little, becoming weaker. I thought I would have more
      time left, but it is too late now. My whole body is shaking as I write this.
      I will soon fall and become like the others. But I still can save my son. I
      have to hurry. He is my last hope. He will be okay, I know. He is a smart boy.
      He can get out of this and save the remains of the town. Good luck, my dear.
      I love you. '
    itemImage: {fileID: 0}
    showTooltipSprite: 0
